Subject: [PATCH] tunipip6: release the route in the encap exception path

nss_tunipip6_encap_exception() looks up an IPv4 route for every exception
packet, but when the route does not point to the tunnel (decap direction)
the packet is handed to netif_receive_skb() without ip_rt_put(), leaking a
dst reference per packet.  Leaked dsts can never be freed once the route
cache entry is replaced, so ip_dst_cache grows (SUnreclaim leak).

---
--- a/tunipip6/nss_connmgr_tunipip6.c
+++ b/tunipip6/nss_connmgr_tunipip6.c
@@ -198,6 +198,13 @@
 		skb->pkt_type = PACKET_HOST;
 		skb->skb_iif = dev->ifindex;
 		skb->ip_summed = CHECKSUM_NONE;
+
+		/*
+		 * The route was only used to choose the direction; release it,
+		 * or every packet taking this path leaks a dst reference
+		 * (IPv4 dst entries pile up in ip_dst_cache).
+		 */
+		ip_rt_put(rt);
 		netif_receive_skb(skb);
 		return;
 	}
